    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1263">

                <pb facs="0874" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 313.115/3.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Hamm.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 103.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received a
                    communication, dated May 5, 1913, from Mr. Frank L. Peckham, attorney at law, of
                    Washington, <pb facs="0875" n="759" xml:id="pg759"/> D. C, saying that the San
                    Luis Mining Company, one of the properties owned by Mrs. Phoebe A. Hearst,
                    having headquarters at Socavon, District of San Dimas, Durango, Mexico, has been
                    forced to contribute the sum of $2,500, Mexican, to the so-called
                    Constitutionalists in that district.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to protest unofficially against the action of the so-called
                    Constitutionalists to the Constitutionalist authorities.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
